<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hod Hill</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hod Hill is a large <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> hillfort near Blandford Forum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dorset">Dorset</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, and one of the strongholds of the Durotriges. After the Roman invasion of 43 CE it was captured, and a Roman fort was built inside one corner of its ramparts, garrisoned by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">legionaries</a> and auxiliary cavalry for several years. Its well-preserved earthworks make it an important site for studying the conquest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hod-hill.jpg" alt="Hod Hill" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jim Champion · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Northern_side_of_the_hillfort_on_Hod_Hill_-_geograph.org.uk_-_242753.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
